1
00:00:00,439 --> 00:00:03,089
Two teams build systems separately, in fact,

2
00:00:03,289 --> 00:00:05,519
even in different GCP projects,

3
00:00:05,650 --> 00:00:08,659
and suddenly they need to talk to each other privately.

4
00:00:08,779 --> 00:00:11,770
This is exactly where VPC peering is going to use.

5
00:00:11,920 --> 00:00:13,350
Let's see how we can do that.

6
00:00:13,449 --> 00:00:16,000
I'm in the console, and I have two projects.

7
00:00:16,170 --> 00:00:20,530
One is hpc3 and another one is hpc2.

8
00:00:20,700 --> 00:00:24,040
Earlier in the previous clip, we have added both of

9
00:00:24,040 --> 00:00:26,500
these two projects to the shared VPC.

10
00:00:26,639 --> 00:00:31,399
I've removed that and deleted all the instances so that these are clean now.

11
00:00:31,520 --> 00:00:35,119
What we're going to do is we're going to create two different

12
00:00:35,119 --> 00:00:38,759
networks in each of these projects, and then we're going to do

13
00:00:38,759 --> 00:00:40,580
the VPC peering between them.

14
00:00:40,720 --> 00:00:46,270
So for that, come down to the hpc2 and let's create one new VPC network.

15
00:00:46,549 --> 00:00:48,509
Say here, Create VPC network.

16
00:00:48,630 --> 00:00:51,630
I give the name as project‑2‑vpc.

17
00:00:51,840 --> 00:00:57,110
Similarly, for the subnet, I'm going to give the name as project‑2‑vpc‑subnet.

18
00:00:57,229 --> 00:00:58,310
In the IP range,

19
00:00:58,470 --> 00:01:05,910
I'm going to select the IP range as 10.1.0.0, and I'm going to say Create.

20
00:01:06,419 --> 00:01:10,699
Select the region as asia‑southeast1 and say Create.

21
00:01:10,860 --> 00:01:14,019
Now on similar lines, go to the other project.

22
00:01:14,099 --> 00:01:17,949
Here also, I go down to my VPC.

23
00:01:18,379 --> 00:01:21,940
Here as well, I'm going to create one VPC network.

24
00:01:22,059 --> 00:01:26,059
I'm going to call this as project‑3‑vpc.

25
00:01:26,269 --> 00:01:32,300
On similar lines, I'm going to give the name as project‑3‑vpc‑subnet,

26
00:01:32,379 --> 00:01:35,949
select the region as asia‑southeast1,

27
00:01:36,069 --> 00:01:43,349
select the IP range as 10.2.0.0 and say Create.

28
00:01:43,470 --> 00:01:46,389
Now both the project has their VPC.

29
00:01:46,589 --> 00:01:49,910
Now it's time to create a VPC peering.

30
00:01:50,029 --> 00:01:55,550
So I'm going back into the project 2, and I'm creating a VPC network peering.

31
00:01:55,919 --> 00:01:59,129
In the VPC network peering, click on Create connection,

32
00:01:59,410 --> 00:02:07,400
give the name as project2‑to‑3, that is the connection. Select the VPC network,

33
00:02:07,730 --> 00:02:13,130
that is project‑2‑vpc, and where we want to do this peering into another project.

34
00:02:13,250 --> 00:02:16,050
So I need another project ID.

35
00:02:16,279 --> 00:02:21,419
So I come down here, copy the name of my project ID, say this,

36
00:02:21,440 --> 00:02:25,320
and it will ask me to give the name of the VPC there.

37
00:02:26,399 --> 00:02:27,259
Say Create.

38
00:02:27,759 --> 00:02:31,800
Now this will create the peering from project 2 to project 3.

39
00:02:32,000 --> 00:02:35,149
Now to check whether this is working or not,

40
00:02:35,199 --> 00:02:39,740
I'm going to create two instances, one in each project.

41
00:02:39,919 --> 00:02:42,509
So I come down here, Create instance.

42
00:02:42,759 --> 00:02:44,679
Now while I'm going to create the instance,

43
00:02:44,800 --> 00:02:49,639
I'm going to choose a specific network here under the Networking setting.

44
00:02:49,850 --> 00:02:52,300
The network is project‑2‑vpc.

45
00:02:52,960 --> 00:02:58,639
Second project, I'm using the project‑2‑vpc as my network and say Create.

46
00:02:58,839 --> 00:03:04,259
I go to the project 3, and I'm going to create one instance here as well.

47
00:03:04,589 --> 00:03:05,514
Create instance,

48
00:03:05,875 --> 00:03:09,654
select the region. Under the Networking field, we're going to select

49
00:03:09,654 --> 00:03:15,785
here the network as our project‑3‑vpc and say Create.

50
00:03:16,505 --> 00:03:20,024
Now we have an instance in each of these projects,

51
00:03:20,035 --> 00:03:24,764
and I want to connect project 2 to project 3 using the peering.

52
00:03:24,884 --> 00:03:29,929
Now I have to just test so I can just come down here and say

53
00:03:30,130 --> 00:03:35,750
SSH. We also need to create the VPC peering from project 3 to

54
00:03:35,750 --> 00:03:37,740
project 2, so let's do that as well.

55
00:03:37,910 --> 00:03:42,460
Say Create connection and give the name as peering‑project‑3‑to‑2.

56
00:03:42,789 --> 00:03:45,229
Select the network and select the project ID.

57
00:03:45,490 --> 00:03:47,990
Select the VPC name and say Create.

58
00:03:48,089 --> 00:03:48,250
Now,

59
00:03:48,320 --> 00:03:52,710
if I do the SSH from this project 2 and in the project

60
00:03:53,089 --> 00:03:56,729
3, the VM IP address is 10.2.0.2.

61
00:03:56,850 --> 00:03:58,190
So I can just say here,

62
00:03:58,330 --> 00:04:06,500
ping 10.2.0.2, and see we are able to make a connection to

63
00:04:06,500 --> 00:04:12,779
the project 3 instance from project 2, because we have done the VPC peering.

64
00:04:12,899 --> 00:04:15,669
The network can now talk internally using private IP.
